  "caption": "Quinn's Achilles hurt, so Quinn rested for two weeks straight. It still hurt. So Quinn tried the opposite — hill sprints.\n\nTendon pain sits on a spectrum, from freshly irritated to long-standing, and the stage helps decide how much load the tendon needs. It's often not simply inflammation that rest will settle.\n\nWhat can help: ease off what provokes it during a flare (without stopping everything), try isometric holds when it's irritable, progress to slow heavier loading, stay within a tolerable pain window, and remember a scan is only part of the picture.\n\nGet it checked if pain came on suddenly after an injury, there's a visible gap, you're losing function, you feel unwell, or there's no change after 8–12 weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
